 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:46:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/71] Rename the user-facing product surface to Suffice

The fork ships under its own name, so every surface a user actually sees
now says Suffice: the binary and its clap help, the config home
(SUFFICE_HOME, ~/.suffice, and the in-repo .suffice project folder),
approval prompts, rate-limit copy, the npm package, and the docs.

The internal crate graph keeps the codex-* names. Renaming ~57k
identifiers would permanently break merges from openai/codex while
changing nothing a user can observe. CI, Bazel release tooling, the
Apache NOTICE, and genuine OpenAI API references are untouched for the
same reason.

Two functional fixes fall out of the binary rename: the agents overview
resolved a sibling `codex` executable, and the Windows Defender event
classifier matched `codex.exe`; both now look for `suffice`.
